<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11564" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crĕpundĭa</span></b> ,
			ōrum, n.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				rattle;</i> and specif., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Most freq., <i>a child's rattle</i> (cf.
			Ruhnk. ad <i><span class="en">Ter. Eun. 4, 6, 15</span></i>), <i><span class="en">Plaut. Mil. 5,
				6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Rud. 4, 4, 37</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 3,
			7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Cist. 3, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 4</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">1, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Brut. 91, 313</span></i> Jahn ad loc.;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				11, 51, 112, § 270</span></i>.—Hence,
			‡ 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">A CREPVNDIIS,</span>”
				<i>from childhood</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 1183</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>An amulet</i>, <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p.
				310, 19</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Rattling musical instruments</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 30,
				1, 9</span></i>.</div>
